# Monorepo Consolidation: All Sub-Projects → `apps/`

Move every sub-project into `apps/` as a regular directory. Eliminate all submodules and the `mudanzas-coral` alias.

## Target Structure

```
apps/
├── devops-shop/    (was submodule → regular dir)
├── zerodelay/      (was submodule → regular dir, absorbs mudanzas-coral)
├── zero-chaos/     (rename from reformas)
├── zerovanity/     (move from src/features/projects/salon)
├── crypto/         (move from src/features/projects/crypto)
├── ecommerce/      (move from src/features/projects/ecommerce)
├── analytics/      (move from src/features/projects/analytics)
```

`src/features/projects/` will be **deleted entirely** after migration.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Git Submodule Removal

Remove all 3 submodules and convert to regular directories.

#### Submodules to remove:
| Submodule | Path | Repo |
|---|---|---|
| devops-shop | `apps/devops-shop` | DevOps.Shop.git |
| zerodelay | `apps/zerodelay` | ZeroDelay.git |
| mudanzas-coral | `src/features/projects/mudanzas-coral` | Portfolio.git |

**Commands:**
```
git submodule deinit -f apps/devops-shop apps/zerodelay src/features/projects/mudanzas-coral
git rm -f apps/devops-shop apps/zerodelay src/features/projects/mudanzas-coral
rm -rf .git/modules/apps/devops-shop .git/modules/apps/zerodelay .git/modules/src/features/projects/mudanzas-coral
```
Then re-add the content as regular directories (copy from cached content or re-clone).

---

### Phase 2: Move & Rename Directories

| From | To | Action |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/reformas` | `apps/zero-chaos` | Rename |
| `src/features/projects/salon` | `apps/zerovanity` | Move (strip `.git`) |
| `src/features/projects/crypto` | `apps/crypto` | Move (strip `.git`) |
| `src/features/projects/ecommerce` | `apps/ecommerce` | Move |
| `src/features/projects/analytics` | `apps/analytics` | Move |
| `src/features/projects/mudanzas-coral` | _(deleted)_ | Content absorbed by `apps/zerodelay` |

After this phase, `src/features/projects/` is deleted.

